.TH SUPIVPN-PROFILE 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn-profile \- initialize a wrapping key or create a VPN client profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-profile
.B \-init
.BI \-server-key " file"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B supivpn-profile
.BI \-out " file"
.BI \-server-key " file"
.BI \-template " file"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly initializes a tls-crypt-v2 server wrapping key, preserving an
existing key, or issues a client profile into a new mode-0600 file.
Profile contents are never written to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-init
Initialize or validate the server wrapping key. Mutually exclusive with \-out.
.TP
.BI \-server-key " file"
Wrapping key path. Default: /var/lib/supivpn/tls-crypt-v2-server.key.
For the combined Debian installation, explicitly select
/etc/supivpn/keys/tls-crypt-v2-server.key and follow the documented ownership rules.
.TP
.BI \-openvpn " file"
Absolute OpenVPN executable path. Default: /usr/sbin/openvpn.
.TP
.BI \-template " file"
Client template. Default: /etc/supivpn/client.ovpn.template.
.TP
.BI \-out " file"
Create a historical unbound client profile at this path.
This output is refused by v0.9.0 listeners. Current users must obtain a
SAML-authorized bound profile through the controller.
.TP
.BI \-secret-arn " arn"
Use an AWS Secrets Manager cluster wrapping key. Only valid with \-init.
This is an explicit external credential operation, not part of package setup.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH NOTES
The initial implementation requires the tested OpenVPN Community 2.7.8.
Package installation never invokes this command or creates keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
